{"name":"French Moire","hex":"#9fbbc3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"french","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prepare food by cutting it into strips.","To kiss (another person) while inserting one’s tongue into the other person's mouth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/french"},{"term":"moire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Originally, a fine textile fabric made of the hair of an Asiatic goat.","Any textile fabric to which a watered appearance is given."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moiré pattern","blocks":[{"text":"In mathematics, physics, and art, a moiré pattern or moiré fringe is a large-scale wave interference pattern that can be produced when a partially opaque ruled pattern with transparent gaps is overlaid on another similar pattern. For the moiré interference pattern to appear, the two patterns must not be completely identical, but rather displaced, rotated, or have slightly different pitch."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Moir%C3%A9_pattern.svg/330px-Moir%C3%A9_pattern.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moir%C3%A9_pattern"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Divers_-_Illustrated_London_News_Feb_6_1873-2.PNG/500px-Divers_-_Illustrated_London_News_Feb_6_1873-2.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Divers_-_Illustrated_London_News_Feb_6_1873-2.PNG/1280px-Divers_-_Illustrated_London_News_Feb_6_1873-2.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Divers_-_Illustrated_London_News_Feb_6_1873-2.PNG/500px-Divers_-_Illustrated_London_News_Feb_6_1873-2.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign